The error message DOMException: The operation is insecure typically occurs when a web page script tries to access a browser API or perform an action that is disallowed for security reasons, such as accessing a database that is not on the same domain as the web page.

It is possible that the indexedDB.databases() call is being prevented by the browser’s same-origin policy, which restricts scripts from accessing resources not on the same domain as the page. To avoid this error, you should either ensure that the script is running on the same domain as the database or you could use a server-side language to access the database and call that via AJAX request.

